# The coefficient prime selected by a p-adic embedding is prime

Theorem statement: `MTT.Eigenform.coefficientPrime_isPrime`
(`bf91feb0-0052-4fd0-bbfb-414f22f43b6b`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-20.

Proof: submission `d75ffd3d-fe76-43b7-8d3f-9103bed14839`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-20 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

The ideal of the eigenform coefficient ring selected by an embedding
into $\mathbf C_p$ is a prime ideal.

## Explanation of the source proof

By definition, the coefficient prime is the inverse image of the maximal ideal of the valuation ring
of `C_p`. A maximal ideal is prime, and the comap of a prime ideal along a ring homomorphism is
prime. The uploaded theorem is at `_root_.solution`.

